{"record": "turn", "turn": 4, "seconds": 5.645, "response_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "stop_reason": "tool_use", "stop_details": null, "blocks": ["thinking", "tool_use"], "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 2326}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 2326, "cache_read_input_tokens": 8613, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 856, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 397}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "tools": [{"id": "toolu_01VRL9RdYbHnsxQrQnJ1VNQg", "name": "submit_answer", "arguments": {"answer": "No. The dSph gamma-ray limit uses a one-sided 95% CL criterion: 2Δ ln L = 2.71 (TS drop of 2.71) from the maximum. The nuisance parameter profiled is each dwarf's J-factor, via a Gaussian prior on log10 of the J normalization s (J = sJ0). The AMS-02 antiproton limit uses ΔQ = Δ(-2 ln L) = 3.84, the nominal 95% interval threshold for one parameter, taking its upper endpoint. The paper notes this differs from the one-sided 2.71 prescription. The nuisance parameter profiled is the Galactic diffusive-halo half-height L. It has a Gaussian penalty in log10 L (L̂ = 4.96 kpc, σ = 0.197) and is profiled over 1–12 kpc.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.2"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "5"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.3"}]}, "status": "answer", "error_kind": null, "seconds": 0.0}]}
{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261116T082359Z_dev-02_staged_ed32", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "No. The dSph gamma-ray limit uses a one-sided 95% CL criterion: 2Δ ln L = 2.71 (TS drop of 2.71) from the maximum. The nuisance parameter profiled is each dwarf's J-factor, via a Gaussian prior on log10 of the J normalization s (J = sJ0). The AMS-02 antiproton limit uses ΔQ = Δ(-2 ln L) = 3.84, the nominal 95% interval threshold for one parameter, taking its upper endpoint. The paper notes this differs from the one-sided 2.71 prescription. The nuisance parameter profiled is the Galactic diffusive-halo half-height L. It has a Gaussian penalty in log10 L (L̂ = 4.96 kpc, σ = 0.197) and is profiled over 1–12 kpc.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.2"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "5"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.3"}]}, "turns": 4, "seconds": 9.98, "tool_calls": 4, "tool_result_chars": 19377, "input_tokens": 10, "output_tokens": 1179, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 2326, "cache_read_input_tokens": 23044, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-16T08:24:09+00:00"}
